WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.070
London is the second largest city in Europe,
and underneath this bustling city is one of

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.060
the oldest and largest networks of train tunnels
in the world.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.350
But that's not the only huge, old structure
located beneath the city of London.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:20.199
Below even the deepest underground metro stations
of this historic city, there's a whole artificial

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:26.099
world of surveillance cyborgs, impossible
architecture, and stomach churning nutritional

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:27.439
supplements.

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:34.540
So be sure to mind the gap, because we're
about to take you on a tour of SCP-1678, also

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.500
known as UnLondon.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:42.350
SCP-1678 is located one kilometer below the
city of London, England.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:47.580
From all appearances, it seems to be an exact
copy of the city, though aesthetically, it's

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.820
more in line with how it was around the turn
of the 20th century.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:56.620
Gas streetlights stand on every corner, and
the modern skyscrapers of the business district

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:00.260
are recreated in the style of Victorian architecture.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.570
The epicenter of construction appears to be
the houses of parliament, which is evidenced

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:09.940
by the more unfinished and flawed the city
becomes further out from the center one goes.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.719
Some of the buildings are made of nonsensical
materials like copper pipes, and some of the

00:01:14.719 --> 00:01:19.700
'gas lamps' are nothing more than a ball of
disembodied light floating atop a metal pole.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.689
The first big question that the Foundation
had upon discovering this location was, of

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:28.009
course, why on earth was it created?

00:01:28.009 --> 00:01:32.829
And they wouldn’t have to look far, as an
explanation of this bizarre mirror city plays

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:34.530
automatically upon entering -

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:35.750
“My fellow citizen.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:40.600
If you are hearing this tape, then the world
as we knew it has finished.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:46.790
The sky has broken, the ground heaves with
the tramp of terrible feet, and all the horror

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:52.170
and madness from the dark corners of the world
has broken free to exact its vengeance on

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.201
the world of Man.

00:01:55.201 --> 00:02:00.630
Evil has raised its bloody flag upon all nations
of the world and crowed its unholy victory

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.600
to the broken sky.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.829
Yes, this is the end.

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:07.590
But there is a new hope.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:11.989
Welcome to UnLondon, a city of the survivors,
a city of the free.

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:17.040
Together, fellow citizen, we will wait and
prepare for the new beginning, the grand new

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.950
world that is soon to come.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.010
Let the world above burn.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.420
We will endure.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.099
Let the monsters have their world.

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:26.769
We will prepare.

00:02:26.769 --> 00:02:27.769
We will wait.

00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:32.040
And I tell you, citizen, that there will be
a new morning.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.700
And you will emerge from UnLondon, and stand
blinking in the sun.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:41.150
And on that day, citizen, there shall be a
new order, as we raise the Union Flag over

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:42.709
the entire world.

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:46.540
I welcome you to UnLondon, the Last City.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.799
And the first.”

00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:52.799
From this message, it seems that this mirror
city was built to be a refuge for survivors

00:02:52.799 --> 00:02:58.380
of an apocalyptic scenario, but the SCP Foundation
had no knowledge of such a plan.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:03.060
In fact, it's still unknown who created this
place, or how they did it.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.560
The one fact that was evident to the Foundation
was that even though this strange place was

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:12.980
intended to be a safe haven, it was far too
poorly constructed to actually act as one.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:18.270
Illumination was unreliable, and most of the
buildings were damp and infested with mold.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:22.660
It's also unclear to the Foundation where
the oxygen and gas supply of UnLondon was

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.750
coming from.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:28.310
Throughout the day, the loudspeakers around
UnLondon play automated messages such as “No

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:33.129
one is safe from the influence of memetic
beings.”, “Bryson’s Home for the Poor

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:39.090
is here to help.” and “Crime will not
be tolerated in UnLondon...The tormentors

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.879
of society will become its defenders.”

00:03:41.879 --> 00:03:47.719
At the end of every hour that passes, the
speakers announce the time, followed by “...and

00:03:47.719 --> 00:03:48.909
all is well”.

00:03:48.909 --> 00:03:54.739
When the SCP Foundation first entered UnLondon,
it was unknown whether or not any living things

00:03:54.739 --> 00:03:56.140
inhabited the city.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:00.670
On first investigation, it seemed from its
state of disrepair that the city had been

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:01.790
long abandoned.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:07.190
But soon the foundation met their first inhabitant
of the underground city.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:11.459
Mobile Task Force members were inspecting
the area around the houses of parliament when

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:13.560
they discovered what looked to be a bank.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.470
As they approached the doors, they heard the
following announcement over the nearby loudspeakers:

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.970
“Citizen, you are entering a restricted
area.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.270
Have your authorization papers ready.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.960
A Bobby will arrive to escort you shortly.”

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:32.690
This signaled the approach of SCP-1678-A,
also known as 'the bobbies'.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:39.100
A single instance of SCP-1678-A appeared with
the unmistakable sound of a police whistle,

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:43.420
and as soon as it arrived it started attacking
the members of the task force.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.800
Another announcement came over the speakers-
‘‘Police!

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.530
Halt, criminal!’’

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:51.870
The bobbies are the main threat to visitors
in UnLondon, and they will attack on sight

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.569
with any improvised weapon they can find.

00:04:54.569 --> 00:04:59.440
True to their name, they are all dressed in
uniforms consistent with those of London city

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.350
police officers from the Victorian era.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:06.970
What sets them apart from their historical
counterparts, is their construction.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:12.560
These beings are made out of human corpses,
crudely dismembered at the joints and re-assembled

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:17.319
using metal hinges and bolts, with their heads
wrapped in bandages.

00:05:17.319 --> 00:05:21.949
Bobbies are extremely hard to kill, with only
high-caliber rounds and explosive weapons

00:05:21.949 --> 00:05:24.310
being effective at putting them down.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:28.470
Autopsies of dead bobbies have shown that
underneath the police uniform, the bobbies

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.530
all wear prison inmate-style jumpsuits.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:36.470
This adds a chilling context to the announcement
about 'the tormentors of society becoming

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:42.610
its defenders'- it appears that the bobbies
are the reanimated bodies of prisoners.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:46.789
In addition to the bobbies, the Foundation
cataloged two additional forms of artificial

00:05:46.789 --> 00:05:49.169
life present within UnLondon.

00:05:49.169 --> 00:05:55.979
First are SCP-1678-B, or Eyes in the Sky,
hybrid bio-mechanical birds made of flesh

00:05:55.979 --> 00:05:58.699
with an exoskeleton of copper wiring.

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:04.000
Some of these creatures are covered in a deteriorating
outer layer of plastic and feathers, suggesting

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.000
that they were originally meant to resemble
pigeons.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:12.139
As their name suggests, eyes in the sky serve
as a type of surveillance drone, and while

00:06:12.139 --> 00:06:17.530
they have no offensive capabilities, they
still pose a significant threat to the Foundation.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:21.880
It's still unclear whether they're able to
communicate with or summon the bobbies, but

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:25.250
the SCP takes no chances.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:34.030
The last 'life form' present in SCP-1678 is
the strangest and the most frightening - SCP-1678-C,

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.100
known as the wretch.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:40.620
The wretch has only ever been encountered
outside the zone which is now under SCP Foundation

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:45.410
control, and it's uncertain how many instances
of this being exist.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:50.550
The wretch resembles an old woman, or sometimes
old man, dressed in filthy rags.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:54.690
The wretch sits at street corners holding
a begging tray, and will attempt to elicit

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:57.800
pity from anyone who happens to walk by.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.470
The wretch will ask for food or money, but
if food is supplied, it will start weeping

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:05.449
before vanishing into a puff of black smoke.

00:07:05.449 --> 00:07:09.919
On a few occasions, audio notices playing
on the city's loudspeakers have alluded to

00:07:09.919 --> 00:07:12.660
this being, saying “Do not pity the Wretch.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:16.830
Allow them to pay the price of their betrayal
for all eternity.”

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:21.819
The current Foundation protocol with regards
to the wretch… is to not engage with it

00:07:21.819 --> 00:07:22.819
at all.

00:07:22.819 --> 00:07:27.069
In addition to the bobbies, the eyes in the
sky, and the wretches, there's another strange

00:07:27.069 --> 00:07:29.720
component to the world of UnLondon.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:34.640
Throughout the city, in any area designed
for human habitation, the Foundation discovered

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.039
multiple machines that resembled modern gas
pumps.

00:07:38.039 --> 00:07:43.819
These machines are fitted with coin slots
and rubber hoses that, when coins are inserted,

00:07:43.819 --> 00:07:48.220
dispense a porridge-like substance advertised
as 'Dr. Goody's Wonderfood'.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:53.300
According to posters around the city, Wonderfood
is a meal replacement supplement, supposedly

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.440
containing all of the required nutrients for
survival.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:01.000
Wonderfood also appears to be the only food
source available in UnLondon.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:05.220
Despite the claims by various posters around
the city that Wonderfood ‘Contains all the

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.990
nutrients you need!’ and ‘Completely restores
health and vitality!’examination of the

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:15.539
substance has revealed that it is, much like
the rest of UnLondon, unsuitable for sustaining

00:08:15.539 --> 00:08:16.539
life.

00:08:16.539 --> 00:08:20.250
Tests have confirmed that Wonderfood is a
synthetic starch gel heavily enriched with

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:25.849
various minerals, vitamins, fats and bulking
agents, and it contains artificially engineered

00:08:25.849 --> 00:08:27.390
DNA helix structures.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:32.320
While it does contain all the elements required
for short-term survival, consuming the product

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:37.940
for longer than 6 weeks will result in severe
malnutrition and eventually scurvy.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:42.060
Further tests have shown that Wonderfood also
contains certain psychoactive properties.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:46.820
The porridge contains a mixture of unknown
molecular compounds which, through regular

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:52.050
consumption, make subjects calmer, less anxious,
and less likely to resist authority.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:56.410
It also seems to have been engineered to cause
withdrawal symptoms that set in if a person

00:08:56.410 --> 00:09:00.620
stops eating it, symptoms which include headaches
and depression.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:05.010
Foundation personnel are forbidden to consume
Wonderfood, but the substance is highly attractive

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:10.800
to instances of SCP-1678-B and 1678-C.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:15.660
Like most things in UnLondon, the quality
of Wonderfood varies wildly, with some dispensers

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:20.360
putting out a product that is so degraded
that it can cause sickness, deformities, or

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.240
even death in the consumer.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:27.320
But strangely, the Foundation has also recorded
a type of unknown colorful mollusk which feeds

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.130
on spillage from the Wonderfood dispensers.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:33.390
At present, UnLondon is only partially contained.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:38.579
Mobile Task Forces Tau-4 and Epsilon-6 have
succeeded in establishing a perimeter around

00:09:38.579 --> 00:09:45.350
the Hyde Park district where they have managed
to stop any incursion from SCP-1678-A. Even

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:49.820
though this is the only area that is fully
under Foundation control, explorations have

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:52.830
been conducted of buildings outside that perimeter.

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:57.240
The investigations are vital for the Foundation's
main purpose in UnLondon, which is figuring

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:02.060
out who built it, and exactly what kind of
event this underground mirror city was meant

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:03.399
to prepare for.

00:10:03.399 --> 00:10:08.170
The interior of the Natural History Museum
yielded particularly strange insights into

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.820
the purpose of UnLondon.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:14.029
For the most part, the museum is close to
how it appears in the above ground, but with

00:10:14.029 --> 00:10:16.070
one key difference.

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:21.260
The task force investigating the museum discovered
an exhibit called 'The Fall of Man', exactly

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.220
where the Darwin Wing should have been.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:28.310
The exhibit, as its name suggests, details
the apocalyptic scenario that would've theoretically

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:31.399
driven people underground into UnLondon.

00:10:31.399 --> 00:10:37.209
But, to everyone’s surprise, its dioramas
and displays didn't depict an asteroid impact,

00:10:37.209 --> 00:10:39.510
plague, or nuclear armageddon.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:43.980
To the Foundation task force members, the
scenes of destruction depicted in the exhibit

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:46.010
were far more familiar.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:51.610
They recognized the reptilian form of SCP-682,
the ordinary-looking brownstone basement door

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:58.890
that serves as a gateway to SCP-2317, and,
most chillingly, the imposing many-eyed figure

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.050
of the Scarlet King.

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:05.470
These were only some of the known Keter class
SCPs depicted in the museum exhibit.

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:10.740
It was clear that even though the SCP Foundation
hadn't built this city, whoever did knew a

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.620
lot about the SCP Foundation's activities.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:18.270
It's believed by the Foundation that whoever
or whatever created UnLondon still resides

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:22.850
in the houses of parliament, and the ultimate
goal of the task forces is to infiltrate the

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:23.850
building.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:27.650
But in order to do that, they will first need
to find where the bobbies are made and halt

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:28.810
their production.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:32.950
It's believed that Bryson's Home for the Poor
is where they originate from, but it's unclear

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:38.700
exactly where the materials to make them come
from, nor is it clear just how they're produced.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:43.839
Ultimately, the Foundation's goal is to catalog
the entire city, and, once they have stopped

00:11:43.839 --> 00:11:49.320
the production of more bobbies, MTF Tau-4
and Epsilon-6 will storm the houses of parliament

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:52.070
and contain whatever force has created UnLondon.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:57.490
But, London is a very big city, and UnLondon
is just as big.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:02.850
So, there's no telling what else they might
find exploring this bizarre location.

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:09.611
Now go check out “SCP - 035 - The Possessive
Mask” and “SCP - 2935 - O, Death” for

00:12:09.611 --> 00:12:12.280
more chilling stories from the SCP Foundation!

